+---
+id: dl-003-applypatch-rejects-sparse-patches-and-undefined-values
+type: decision-log
+title: "applyPatch rejects sparse patches and undefined values"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+## Context
+The RFC requires every operation to be an object and `add`, `replace` and `test` to carry a `value`.
+`applyPatch` used `Array.reduce`, which skips holes, and tested `value` with `hasOwn`, which accepts
+`undefined`, so two invalid patches were accepted.
+
+## Decision
+Operations are applied with a `for...of` loop, so a hole is seen as `undefined` and rejected. A `value`
+of `undefined` counts as missing, since `undefined` is not a JSON value.
+
+## Consequences
+Both inputs now throw `Error` and leave the document untouched. Valid JSON patches are unaffected.
